# Task branch + PR + merge

When implementing a `TASKS.md` task (or the user says "next task", "ship TASK N", or "make a plan" for a ⬜/⏳ task), follow `.cursor/skills/ship-task/SKILL.md`.

- One task per branch. Never commit task work to `main`.
- Branch: `task/<id>-<slug>` (example: `task/10-tutorial`).
- After acceptance criteria and quality gates: commit, push, open a PR, merge it, return to `main`.
- That standing ask is merge permission for that task's PR only. Still use `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch`. Then `git checkout main && git pull && git fetch --prune`.
- Do not start the next ⬜ task on the same branch.
- `gh repo create` and GitHub Pages still need an explicit human ask.
